<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>What cookies are</h2>
  <p>Cookies are small data files stored on your device to support website functionality and preferences.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Strictly necessary cookies</h2>
  <p>These cookies are always active and required for security, session continuity, and core website operation.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Optional cookies requiring consent</h2>
  <p>Analytics and third-party embedded content categories remain off unless you provide explicit consent.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>How consent works</h2>
  <p>The banner allows Accept, Reject, and Manage Preferences actions. No implied consent is assumed.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>How to withdraw consent</h2>
  <p>You can withdraw optional consent at any time from <a href="/legal/cookie-preferences/">Cookie Preferences</a> in the footer or legal area.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Browser controls</h2>
  <p>You can also control cookies through your browser settings. Browser blocking may affect functionality.</p>
</div>
